PIMID: run one REP string iteration per block execution while a TCG plugin is loaded

QEMU 10 and later translate a REP MOVS/STOS/LODS/CMPS/SCAS as a loop that runs up to
65535 iterations inside one execution of the block. A plugin then sees one block (and
one instruction) followed by up to 65535 memory accesses. ZSim ends a phase, and frees
the timing events of the last one, only at a block boundary, so a large memset or
memcpy piled all its events into one phase and overflowed ZSim's 256 MB global heap
(PIMID gate 12216A). With a plugin loaded, this makes the translator take the
one-iteration path it already uses for icount and single-step: each iteration ends
the block and re-enters the instruction, as QEMU 9.2 always did.

Applies to QEMU v11.1.2 (PIMID 1.12.16). Apply inside external/qemu:
    git apply ../qemu-patches/0001-i386-one-rep-iteration-per-block-with-plugins.patch

diff --git a/target/i386/tcg/translate.c b/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
index 2115c5c..42345a2 100644
--- a/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
+++ b/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
@@ -1329,7 +1329,8 @@ static void do_gen_rep(DisasContext *s, MemOp ot, TCGv dshift,
      */
     bool can_loop =
         (!(tb_cflags(s->base.tb) & (CF_USE_ICOUNT | CF_SINGLE_STEP))
-	 && !(s->flags & (HF_TF_MASK | HF_INHIBIT_IRQ_MASK)));
+	 && !(s->flags & (HF_TF_MASK | HF_INHIBIT_IRQ_MASK))
+	 && !s->base.plugin_enabled);
     bool had_rf = s->flags & HF_RF_MASK;
 
     /*
